return {h=3,w=40,cr=190,hc=20,bh=70,gr="slow",eg={"water3"},st={30,65,100,45,25,40},ab={{75,0},{92,0},{142,1}},genus={en="Bivalve Pokémon",es="Pokémon Bivalvo",pt="Pokémon Bivalve"},flavor={en={[1]="Its hard shell repels any kind of attack. It is vulnerable only when its shell is open.",[2]="Its hard shell repels any kind of attack. It is vulnerable only when its shell is open.",[3]="The shell can withstand any attack. However, when it is open, the tender body is exposed.",[4]="It swims facing backward by opening and closing its two-piece shell. It is surprisingly fast.",[5]="Grains of sand trapped in its shells mix with its body fluids to form beautiful pearls.",[6]="Clamping on to an opponent reveals its vulnerable parts, so it uses this move only as a last resort.",[7]="At night, this Pokémon uses its broad tongue to burrow a hole in the seafloor sand and then sleep in it. While it is sleeping, SHELLDER closes its shell, but leaves its tongue hanging out.",[8]="At night, this Pokémon uses its broad tongue to burrow a hole in the seafloor sand and then sleep in it. While it is sleeping, SHELLDER closes its shell, but leaves its tongue hanging out.",[9]="At night, it burrows a hole in the seafloor with its broad tongue to make a place to sleep. While asleep, it closes its shell, but leaves its tongue hanging out.",[10]="It is encased in a shell that is harder than diamond. Inside, however, it is surprisingly tender.",[11]="Its hard shell repels any kind of attack. It is vulnerable only when its shell is open.",[12]="It swims backward by opening and closing its two shells. Its large tongue is always kept hanging out.",[13]="It swims backward by opening and closing its two shells. Its large tongue is always kept hanging out.",[14]="It swims backward by opening and closing its two shells. Its large tongue is always kept hanging out.",[15]="It swims facing backward by opening and closing its two-piece shell. It is surprisingly fast.",[16]="Grains of sand trapped in its shells mix with its body fluids to form beautiful pearls.",[17]="It swims backward by opening and closing its two shells. Its large tongue is always kept hanging out.",[18]="It swims backward by opening and closing its two shells. Its large tongue is always kept hanging out.",[21]="It swims backward by opening and closing its two shells. Its large tongue is always kept hanging out.",[22]="It swims backward by opening and closing its two shells. Its large tongue is always kept hanging out.",[23]="Its hard shell repels any kind of attack. It is vulnerable only when its shell is open.",[24]="Clamping on to an opponent reveals its vulnerable parts, so it uses this move only as a last resort.",[25]="At night, this Pokémon uses its broad tongue to burrow a hole in the seafloor sand and then sleep in it. While it is sleeping, Shellder closes its shell, but leaves its tongue hanging out.",[26]="At night, this Pokémon uses its broad tongue to burrow a hole in the seafloor sand and then sleep in it. While it is sleeping, Shellder closes its shell, but leaves its tongue hanging out.",[27]="The hardness of its shell surpasses the hardness of a diamond. In days gone by, people used the shells to make shields.",[28]="This Pokémon’s tongue is always hanging out. It uses its tongue with great dexterity to dig up sand from the seabed in its search for food.",[29]="The sand that accumulates inside its shell eventually becomes a pearl. But the pearl gets in the way, so it spits it out and discards it.",[30]="Even when its shell is closed, its tongue still hangs out. If you give its tongue a good yank, the shock will cause Shellder to open its shell.",[31]="The shell can withstand any attack. However, when it is open, the tender body is exposed.",[32]="The shell can withstand any attack. However, when it is open, the tender body is exposed.",[33]="It swims facing backward by opening and closing its two-piece shell. It is surprisingly fast.",[34]="Its hard shell repels any kind of attack. It is vulnerable only when its shell is open."},es={[23]="La concha lo protege de cualquier tipo de ataque. Solo es vulnerable cuando se abre.",[24]="Cuando atenaza a sus enemigos, se vuelve vulnerable. Por eso solo utiliza esta técnica como último recurso.",[25]="Por la noche, este Pokémon usa la ancha lengua que tiene para hacer un agujero en el fondo del mar y echarse a dormir. Mientras duerme, Shellder cierra la concha, pero deja la lengua por fuera.",[26]="Por la noche, este Pokémon usa la ancha lengua que tiene para hacer un agujero en el fondo del mar y echarse a dormir. Mientras duerme, Shellder cierra la concha, pero deja la lengua por fuera.",[27]="Su concha, más dura que un diamante, se empleaba en la antigüedad para la fabricación de escudos.",[28]="Este Pokémon usa su lengua diestramente para excavar en el fondo del mar y buscar alimento.",[29]="La arena que acumula en su interior termina por transformarse en una perla, pero la escupe porque le supone un estorbo.",[30]="Siempre tiene la lengua fuera, aun con la concha cerrada. Si uno tira de ella con fuerza, la abrirá del susto.",[31]="La dura concha que lo recubre resiste cualquier ataque, por lo que su frágil cuerpo solo queda expuesto cuando esta se abre.",[32]="La dura concha que lo recubre resiste cualquier ataque, por lo que su frágil cuerpo solo queda expuesto cuando esta se abre.",[33]="Nada hacia atrás abriendo y cerrando su concha. Es sorprendentemente rápido.",[34]="La concha lo protege de cualquier tipo de ataque. Solo es vulnerable cuando se abre."},pt="Sua concha dura repele qualquer tipo de ataque. Só fica vulnerável quando a concha está aberta."},evo={{s=90},{s=91,from=90,c={{t="use-item",item=84}}}},moves={[1]={1,33,1,110,18,48,23,128,30,62,39,43,50,58},[2]={1,33,1,110,18,48,23,128,30,62,39,43,50,58},[3]={1,33,1,110,9,48,17,62,25,182,33,43,41,128,49,58},[4]={1,33,1,110,9,48,17,62,25,182,33,43,41,128,49,58},[5]={1,33,1,110,9,48,17,62,25,182,33,43,41,128,49,58},[6]={1,33,1,110,9,48,17